Z||000000||firstfiero||03-09-2001||10:39 AM||||    Did anyone get a bra from this company. It's been on back order for 3 months and now their saying another couple weeks. They make to order every bra. Just seeing if the wait is going to be worth it or if I should go somewhere else. I'm getting a bra to cover up some damage on my hood. Already got a fiero store wolf bra...but I'm not happy with it at all and i need one that goes past my headlights.   ||||reg||9
Z||000001||stsmithgt||03-09-2001||11:15 AM||||Colgan makes a nice bra that fits well and goes past the headlights.  It <I>is</I> more effort to manually roll up the covers over the headlights.  The headlight covers velcro down and they do stay down at speeds over 100 m.p.h.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  You have to unhook the upper and loosen the lower hooks, both in the fender well, to get into the trunk, but it's the type I have and it does look nice.  I got mine through the dealership in a couple of days.  I've spent so much money there, I usually get a good deal on the parts.  I think I paid with tax about 80 bucks.  Well that's my 2¢. I'm outa here. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-09-2001||11:21 AM||||I have a Colgan in my Vette and it is a very good product. Don't know about your new brand.||||reg||1
